  "narrative_llm": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This Dryad dataset has begun to register use in the scholarly record: it has 11 recorded downloads, 43 views, and 1 documented citation/reuse by a 2024 article in <em>Oikos</em>. The evidence points to early-stage uptake rather than broad diffusion, but the presence of a downstream article shows that the dataset is already being used in related ecological research.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This dataset, accompanying work on coordinated distributed experiments in ecology and heterogeneity in effect sizes, shows a modest but clear early impact profile. The strongest signals are usage and reuse: DataCite records 43 views and 11 downloads, and the data have been cited as a dataset by one journal article. That article is also the only captured downstream reuse in the record, indicating that the dataset has moved beyond passive archiving into at least one substantive research use.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The citation landscape is still very small, so the story here is best understood as emerging rather than established. OpenAlex records 1 citation, and the citing work appeared in 2024 in <em>Oikos</em>. With only one citation, the available evidence supports a narrative of initial scholarly uptake, not mature influence.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The surrounding stewardship record suggests the dataset is well-positioned for reuse. It is deposited in Dryad, an open repository with DOI-based persistence, and it is linked to related Zenodo software deposits. Those links indicate an ecosystem of associated research materials that can support transparency and reuse, even though the current impact record remains limited in size.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Public attention outside scholarly channels is minimal in the available record. Event-data and scite coverage are both absent here, so there is no basis for claims of wider online discussion. Overall, this is a lightly used but credibly reused dataset whose impact is currently visible mainly through one downstream ecological article and a small amount of direct repository traffic.</p>",
  "narrative_source": "template"
